language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ bananas: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Five bananas cost three dollars, seven oranges cost five dollars, nine mangoes cost seven dollars, and three apples cost nine dollars. I need to purchase 100 fruits for 100 dollars. All types of fruits need to be purchased, but I do not like bananas and apples, so the number of bananas and apples together should be as small as possible.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/bananas.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ bananas: the number of bananas bought (at least one)
find bananas : int(1..100)
$ oranges: the number of oranges bought (at least one)
find oranges : int(1..100)
$ mangoes: the number of mangoes bought (at least one)
find mangoes : int(1..100)
$ apples: the number of apples bought (at least one)
find apples : int(1..100)

minimising bananas + apples
such that
$ exactly 100 fruits are bought
bananas + oranges + mangoes + apples = 100,
$ the total cost is 100 dollars; each price is scaled by 315 (the lcm of 5, 7 and 9) so that it stays an integer:
$ a banana costs 3/5 dollar, so 189; an orange 5/7, so 225; a mango 7/9, so 245; an apple 9/3, so 945; 100 dollars is 31500
189 * bananas + 225 * oranges + 245 * mangoes + 945 * apples = 31500
